          ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and  $det(A)=0?$ \n\nI. $A$ is invertible\n\nII. $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{4}$\n\nIII. $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,\u21d4\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col)}(A)=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null)}(A)=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is false. A matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$ Since here we have $det(A)=0,$ our matrix $A$ is not invertible.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, since $A$ is *not* invertible, we must have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{4}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not invertible,  it must be $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""
