          ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and  $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5}?$ \n\nI. $A$ is invertible\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(A)=6$\n\nIII. $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,\u21d4\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is true. By the invertible matrix theorem,  $A$ is invertible because $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5}.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since,\n\n$$\n\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5}\\,\u27f9\\,\\text{rank}(A)=\\text{dim(Col}(A))=5.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is invertible,  it must be $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""
