# Instructional account

The learner inspects a square real matrix's supplied determinant, full rank/column space, nonzero homogeneous solution, or explicit nullspace. They infer invertibility (and, for an explicit nullspace, count independent spanning vectors), then judge three statements using the invertible matrix theorem. They select a subset in one five-choice radio field or evaluate Boolean checkbox fields. No matrix inversion or determinant calculation is required.

Evidence: supplied source at basis 5437, lesson tutorial 3522 (Introduction) states that the unique homogeneous solution is zero exactly when nullity is zero, all n columns are pivots, rank is n, and the column space is R^n. Canonical e-5424 decomposes a one-parameter nullspace before judging the statements. q-142358, q-142474, q-141196 use two independent spanning vectors; q-34834 and q-139977 use one. q-141199, q-35425, q-34929 establish singularity from a nonzero homogeneous solution, without determining exact rank. q-141200/q-79349/q-142472 have nonzero determinant; q-141198/q-142473 have determinant zero. q-141201 gives full rank and q-141197 gives full column space. These establish the permitted cases and ordered stages.

Supported/default difficulty: moderate, preserving original labels. Easy and hard have no source-backed workload here and are unsupported. The supplied q-34936 is now labeled moderate but still lacks its answer and solution: retain its evidence, exclude generation. q-142367 has a malformed `lI only` distractor: retain its complete evidence, exclude generation rather than silently change the bank. Fifteen complete supported profiles remain. The older bundled source has only twelve supported profiles and outdated checkbox layouts. Latest source replaces that evidence; it does not replace the repaired implementation.

Fixed features: square real matrices are required by the theorem. Three claims and a five-choice radio bank (or original checkbox layout) preserve the response/workload. A supplied nonzero vector must remain nonzero because the zero vector alone gives no invertibility information. Explicit nullspaces retain the source's one/two parameter count per profile and independent, disjoint column supports, so decomposition and counting stay immediate. Coordinate positions and signs need not be fixed: the theorem is invariant to them. Scalar dimension range 3–7 retains the same inference, with no extra arithmetic. Vector/nullspace dimensions remain the source dimensions to preserve decomposition length. Source bank profiles remain complete; “None” is retained only for q-34834 and q-142358, where the latest source explicitly supplies it.

Observed arrangements are not constraints on answer-bearing assignments. Normal sampling first selects a permitted correct subset from the complete source radio bank, or a three-bit checkbox subset (including empty only with source-backed None). It then selects a compatible given case and chooses each statement's relation so its truth agrees. Allowed statement variations are equality/non-equality, invertible/not invertible, full-rank/below-full rank, zero/nonzero nullspace, and numeric dimension/pivot comparisons already exemplified across these sources. These are conservative same-method extensions, not copied source variants. Each slot keeps its original mathematical object (invertibility, nullity, rank, column space, nullspace, pivots). Truth-bearing numerical comparisons are derived after the case; nonzero-vector cases never assert an unknown exact rank/nullity. Determinant profiles admit zero and nonzero cases; full-rank/full-column-space source profiles remain full as their givens require. Exact nullspace size stays one or two per profile, while the queried dimension/relation can change. Complete banks are preserved and shuffled independently of the key. Normal solutions retain theorem → supplied evidence → three judgments → concluding subset; replay retains every original sentence.

Coverage obligations: every profile must exercise each available subset, each claim both true and false, and every radio key position; None profiles must exercise ordinary-empty and nonempty subsets. Determinant profiles must exercise both cases without recognizable template deciding the answer. Check equal givens with changed statement evidence, and equal statements with determinant zero/nonzero; verify prompt, solution, key, and native grading together. Irrelevant nonzero determinant magnitude/sign and nonzero-vector scaling must preserve answers. Count distinct rendered mathematical instances, not UUIDs, seeds, or choice order. Probe truth masks and key positions within profiles and within determinant cases, before and after shared delivery filtering. A mathematical fact such as “a nonzero null vector implies singular” is the intended inference, not an incidental shortcut.

No generated diagrams/assets are needed. Current supplied images list is empty. Source replay, independent visible-content math checks, actual native option grading, relocation, shared delivery filtering, and UI rendering are separate evidence claims. Learner-specific history/weighted draw is not simulated; captured inventory contains 17 source records and no generated records, so packaging failure has no stored generated instances to reconstruct. Original sources must not be relabeled as generated.
